"stremler" <stremler@rohan.sdsu.edu> wrote:

> (Then I put on my tinfoil hat to escape the
> mind-control lasers...)

> ObTopic: Speaking of which, surely someone has
> suggested a tinfoil hat to be added to netscape?

That could be a really fun item, that could make you
psychically invisible to monsters.

Though it would work both ways, mental attack spells
like charm and cause fear, mental attack scrolls
read like taming, would presumably fail 100% while
wearing a tinfoil hat.

But being psychically shielded is most plus side
stuff.

    Mind flayers could only find you by wandering
    around until you were physically visible.

    That long list of monsters that teleport to your
    side, from leprechauns and nymphs to quest
    nemeses, Demon Princes, and Rodney, would
    instead be reduced to teleporting at random
    until they found you visually.

    If monsters use up manna the way PCs do when
    teleporting, so that the WoY had to stop for
    breath while trying to figure out even off to
    what level you'd gotten, the tinfoil hat could
    become one of the most sought-after artifacts in
    the dungeon.

This in turn would suggest that it be made a bit
scarcer than woodchucks, for game balance.

It might only be found, for example, among the death
drops of monsters that stepped on a polymorph trap
while wearing other magic headgear.

What would happen if you put on a cursed tinfoil hat
doesn't bear considering by the squeamish, though.
You'd be a psychic monster magnet, maybe even
summoning them from their lairs on other levels,
with a low probability per turn. Of course, the RNG
hates my PCs, so:

  You put on the conical helm -- more --
  "Helloooooo, Demogorgon!"

xanthian.

Now if it would only make my PCs psychically
invisible to the malice of the RNG...



